virtio_console: create the ports' init and lock devices

A tty's settings go back to those of its .init device each time it is
first opened. virtio console ports had no .init device, so they always
started out in canonical mode with echo, and there was no way to set
them up once for programs that open them themselves: OpenComputers II's
high-level API sends NUL framed JSON over named ports, which has to go
through unchanged. Set TF_INITLOCK, as uart(4) and ucom(4) do, so
/dev/ttyV*.init and .lock exist and "stty -f /dev/ttyV0.1.init raw"
applies to every later open.

diff --git a/sys/dev/virtio/console/virtio_console.c b/sys/dev/virtio/console/virtio_console.c
index ba8fee849..c240093f1 100644
--- a/sys/dev/virtio/console/virtio_console.c
+++ b/sys/dev/virtio/console/virtio_console.c
@@ -236,7 +236,7 @@ static void	 vtcon_disable_interrupts(struct vtcon_softc *);
 static int	 vtcon_pending_free;
 
 static struct ttydevsw vtcon_tty_class = {
-	.tsw_flags	= 0,
+	.tsw_flags	= TF_INITLOCK,
 	.tsw_open	= vtcon_tty_open,
 	.tsw_close	= vtcon_tty_close,
 	.tsw_outwakeup	= vtcon_tty_outwakeup,
